{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Title: A captivating journey through the Land of the Rising Sun\n\nJust returned from a magical trip to Japan, a land of contrasts where ancient traditions and cutting-edge technology coexist in harmony. From the bustling streets of Tokyo to the serene landscapes of Kyoto, this country offered endless wonders to explore.\n\nIn Tokyo, the neon-lit streets of Shibuya and Shinjuku dazzled us with their energy and vibrancy. Amidst the chaos, we found solace in the peaceful Meiji Shrine, a shrine dedicated to the deified spirits of Emperor Meiji and his wife, Empress Shōken. The tranquil forest surrounding the shrine provided a stark contrast to the city's frenetic pace.\n\nWe also visited the historic Asakusa district, where we marveled at the Sensō-ji, Tokyo's oldest temple, and indulged in delicious street food.\n\nOur trip to Kyoto was a step back in time. We strolled through the picturesque Philosopher's Path, a charming canal-side walk lined with cherry trees, and admired the stunning golden pavilion of Kinkaku-ji. The Fushimi Inari Shrine, with its iconic red torii gates, was a highlight of our trip. We hiked up the mountain, taking in the breathtaking views of the city below.\n\nIn Hakone, we enjoyed a relaxing soak in an onsen, a traditional Japanese hot spring, and took a scenic cruise on Lake Ashi, where we were treated to magnificent views of Mt. Fuji.\n\nJapan's cuisine was a culinary adventure. From savoring fresh sushi at the Tsukiji Fish Market to slurping a bowl of ramen at a local izakaya, every meal was a delight.\n\nJapan's rich culture, warm hospitality, and stunning landscapes left an indelible mark on us. We'll be back to explore more of this beautiful country.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Title", "logprob": -0.007975990884006023}, {"token": ":", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.08805465698242188}, {"token": "cap